A thread that runs on spare time past its request is charged for all of it, however far ahead of the clock that puts it.
A thread that once ran long on spare time would wait for its units as long as it ran, where nobody wanted the time;
a place's virtual time lies at most a span past the clock and its request.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a step of the clock did not charge the thread whose turn it was its units' part
Report: a traced call that moved no time charged the thread whose turn it was
Witness: fuzz bind-turn-later

